 offer student discounts?\n\nYes! Simply head here to apply.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDelayed Interventions [iOS] (https://tutorials.one-sec.app/en/articles/3973762)\nciteturn2search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.3 years ago; Crawled: last week; Delayed interventions have been a highly requested feature for one sec since we introduced Re-Interventions: ... Instead, you have to go through an intervention (e.g. breathing exercise) to unlock more time. ... When adding a new app to one sec, you can directly select if the intervention should be shown immediately (= when opening the target app), after a delay, or if one sec should always ask for the delay.\n\n# Delayed Interventions [iOS]\n\nEdited Tuesday, May 27 2025\n\nDelayed interventions have been a highly requested feature for one sec since we introduced Re-Interventions:\n\nWhat if you could freely use Instagram for 3 minutes, to post a story, or reply to an important message – while being protected from getting stuck in Reels and wasting half an hour without even noticing?\n\nThat’s exactly the idea of Delayed Interventions that are introduced in one sec 4.1 (requires iOS 16 or newer):\n\nInstead of intervening you directly when opening a target app, the intervention is delayed by a time interval set by you:\n\nI recommend setting a low interval (e.g. 1 to 3 minutes) to allow for quick, intentional app usage, and still giving you the pressure to not get distracted.\n\n## What happens when the delayed intervention kicks in?\n\nWhen you reach the limit (e.g. 3 minutes) on your target app, the app will be blocked and you can’t continue to use it. Instead, you have to go through an intervention (e.g. breathing exercise) to unlock more time. Then you will be able to select how much more time you’ll need on the target app.\n\nBesides that, the delay is reset / restarted at every full hour.\n\n## Who should use Delayed Interventions?\n\none sec is always about finding the right balance of frustration: Our interventions are so effective (scientifically proven!) because they are annoying and frustrating.\n\nDifferent users have different use-cases and different app require different interventions for different users.\n\nOur scientific experiments have shown that both Immediate and Delayed Interventions are effective in their own ways:\n\n  * Immediate Interventions work by heavily reducing the amount of open attempts for target apps.\n\n  * Delayed Interventions work by heavily reducing the duration of using target apps.\n\n  * Both intervention types show a similar effectiveness in reducing overall screen time. In the end, you have to find the right tool that works for you!\n\nYou can actually set up both Immediate and Delayed interventions for different apps – some apps might require a more intense (=immediate) intervention (e.g. TikTok, Instagram, …) while others are fine to use with the Delayed Intervention (e.g. Mastodon, Mail App, …).\n\nSo it’s up to you: give it a try and be honest with yourself: which interventions helps you best stick to a intentional usage?\n\n## How to change the Intervention Mode: Immediate vs. Delayed vs. Always Ask\n\nWhen adding a new app to one sec, you can directly select if the intervention should be shown immediately (= when opening the target app), after a delay, or if one sec should always ask for the delay.\n\nYou can also change that setting later on for apps that have already been added to one sec: To do so, open the Overview tab of one sec, and select the app you’d like to edit. Then select Customize → Intervention on App:\n\nHere you can switch between Immediate, Delayed, and Always Ask, and change the time interval of the delay as well.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOpal Help Center (https://help.opalapp.com/)\nciteturn2search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; ⌛How to use Time Limits Set Time Limits to block distracting apps and websites once you reach your cumulative usage. ... 🔥How to gain Streaks and Focus Hours Learn how Streaks and Focus Hours build, why they break, and how to reset them on iOS.🌙How to achieve better Sleep with Opal Use Opal’s updated Sleep features, Open Limits, Schedules, and soundscapes for better rest. ... 🙅‍♀️How to enable App Uninstall Protection Turn on App Uninstall Protection to stop yourself from deleting Opal or other apps.\n\n### Opal Help Center\n\nWelcome, Gem! 💎 Thank you for using Opal. How can we help you make the most of your experience?\n\n[Input: Search help articles here...][Input]\n\nFrequently Asked Questions\n\nWhy isn’t Blocking Working Correctly?How do I make Opal foolproof?Cancelling and refunding Opal ProHow to use Parental ControlsHow to Contact Opal Support\n\nHow to use Opal’s features\n\n💯How does Opal calculate your Score Opal calculates a daily Score by combining your Sleep, Focus, and Rest metrics.\n\n⌚How do I see my daily Screen Time?View your daily, weekly, and monthly Screen Time in Opal, split across distracting and other apps.\n\n🕰️How to use Sessions Start an immediate, non-recurring Session to block distracting apps, with optional Hard Mode and unblock controls.\n\n⏰How to use Schedules Set up Schedules to block or Allow Only apps and websites for a chosen period of time.\n\n⌛How to use Time Limits Set Time Limits to block distracting apps and websites once you reach your cumulative usage.\n\n🔓How to use Open Limit Open Limits cap how many times you may open an app or website each day.\n\n🚨How to use Emergency Pass Redeem your weekly Emergency Pass to unblock apps when a Rule allows no breaks or resets.\n\n⏲️How to use Timer Start a Timer to block apps for a set duration or indefinitely, with an optional Hard Mode.\n\n⬜How to use Allow Only Allow Only blocks every app and website on your device except the ones you explicitly allow.\n\n🌬️How to designate apps as Distracting Mark apps and websites as Distracting so Opal can suggest them for Rules and Autofocus.\n\n🟩How to designate apps as Always Allowed Choose which apps and websites stay available on your device using Opal’s Always Allowed feature.\n\n🟥How to designate apps as Never Allowed Permanently block apps and websites on iOS using Opal’s Never Allowed feature.\n\n🚫How to block Adult Websites Block Adult Websites on iOS either permanently or only during specific times with Opal.\n\n🌴How to Enable Vacation Mode Disable your Opal Rules for a set number of days to take a break from blocking on iOS.\n\n🔥How to gain Streaks and Focus Hours Learn how Streaks and Focus Hours build, why they break, and how to reset them on iOS.\n\n🌙How to achieve better Sleep with Opal Use Opal’s updated Sleep features, Open Limits, Schedules, and soundscapes for better rest.\n\n📖How to access Focus Report Access your Opal Focus Report on iOS to measure focus, track progress, and compare benchmarks.\n\n\nAdvanced Features\n\n💔Why isn’t Blocking Working Correctly?Troubleshoot common Opal blocking scenarios to tell intentional behaviour apart from bugs.\n\n🛡️How do I make Opal foolproof?Combine Opal's locking features to build a tamper-proof setup that resists unblocking and uninstalling.\n\n🧑‍🍼How to use Parental Controls Lock down your child's device with an Opal Passcode and Screen Time Passcode so they can't disable Opal.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOpal FAQ | What is Opal and how does it work? (https://opalapp.com/help/what-is-opal)\nciteturn2search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Digital wellbeing is critical to a healthy lifestyle, and Opal can help you reap the benefits of less daily screen time. ...   * Fully customizable Sessions, Time Limits, and Open Limits ... “Weird to think that an app would make me use my phone less... but Opal is the only thing keeping me focused on deep work days.” — Zach\nOur features include:\n\n  * Detailed analytics on progress, including Focus Reports\n  * The ability to set up Block Lists and Allow Lists featuring the apps and websites of your choice\n  * Fully customizable Sessions, Time Limits, and Open Limits\n  * A Focus Score® that allows users to rate how apps hurt or enhance their focus\n  * Social features that allow you to invite friends and share data with them\n  * Integrations with Shortcut Automations and Focus Filters for added automation\n  * Rewards for reaching milestones on the journey towards better focus\n  * An active Community Forum board to discuss improvements, learn tips and tricks, and be social\n  * Responsive Customer Support\n\n### What happens to my data?\n\nUnlike most apps, Opal works entirely on your phone and personal browsing data never leaves your device. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFAQ | one sec (https://one-sec.app/faq/)\nciteturn2search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Review current pricing upon purchase. ... If you want to block more than one app or use advanced customizations, you can upgrade to one sec pro at affordable prices (with a 1 week free trial).\n\nDoes one sec sell my data?\n\nNo. You can be sure we don't sell or analyze your data. We can't even look at it. We make money by selling the app and subscriptions, not by selling your data.\n\nIs one sec safe?\n\nAbsolutely. one sec focuses on building a high-quality product, not tracking or monetizing your data. All intervention logic runs locally on your device—there's no profiling, no data selling, and no investor pressure to push ads or analytics into the app.\n\nHow much does one sec cost?\n\none sec offers a free version which allows to set up a breathing interruption for one app. For unlimited apps and a large number of helpful features, upgrade to one sec pro. - Monthly: 3,99 € - Anually: 14,99 € - Lifetime: 99,99 € Note: prices differ by region. Review current pricing upon purchase.\n\nWhat happens if I have a question or need help?\n\nNo worries! You find various help articles and tutorials on our website. And when you can't find a solution to your problem, you can contact our customer support anytime. To change the language, update your device's language settings.\n\nDoes one sec contain ads?\n\nNo, there are no ads—even in the free version. Showing ads would make our interruptions less effective – we decided to maximize the impact of our product over maximizing profits.\n\nIs one sec free?\n\nYes! You can use one sec for free with your most addictive app or website to make sure the concept works for you. If you want to block more than one app or use advanced customizations, you can upgrade to one sec pro at affordable prices (with a 1 week free trial). If cost is a barrier, just reach out to customer support—they're happy to help find a solution.\n\nCan I buy one sec for my team / school?\n\nYes, you can! We offer team licenses for as low as 83ct per user per month (billed annually). Proceed to the checkout on our website, select \"Multi-Seat Plan\" and add as many licenses as you need.\n\none sec isn't working—what can I do?\n\nIf you're running into issues with one sec, check out our troubleshooting guides for step-by-step fixes: - iOS - Adroid Most problems come from a setup that isn't fully completed or configured correctly. Once everything is set up properly, one sec should run smoothly. If you still encounter issues, please do not hesitate to reach out to our customer support. We're there to help!\n\nLearn more on our tutorials website.\n\n## Contact us\n\nWe’re here to help you get the most out of one sec. If you have any questions or feedback, please don’t hesitate to reach out.\n\nHelp & tutorials Problems with one sec? Or looking for tips to get the most out of it? Check out our help center.Submit Ideas Tell us how we could make one sec more useful to you or report any bugs you’re encountering.\n\nPress inquiries? Please visit our press page.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWhat’s included in one sec pro? (https://tutorials.one-sec.app/en/articles/3036418)\nciteturn2search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: last week; # What’s included in one sec pro? ... one sec is free to use for everyone, but is limited to target one app: ... ### Why did we increase the price of our lifetime subscription? ... Up to now, from various intervention types, Re-Intervention, the Phone Free Morning , scheduling, block sessions, Focus Filters, healthy alternatives, intention tracking, emotion tracking, integrations with Lengo and Structured, and the various lock functions, etc. – a ton of great tools have been added that weren’t factored into the original pricing.\n\n# What’s included in one sec pro?\n\nEdited Friday, June 19 2026\n\none sec is free to use for everyone, but is limited to target one app:\n\nYou can test for free if the principle behind one sec works for you as well. one sec’s approach is scientifically proven & peer-reviewed, it reduces app usage by 57% on average. On top of that, we have received more than 80'000 5-star ratings on the App Store.\n\nIf you would like to use one sec with multiple apps, it’s time to upgrade: on top of unlimited apps, you’ll get access to a long list of amazing features (see below!).\n\n |  | Free  | Pro (iOS)  | Pro (Android)  | Pro (Desktop Web Browser)\n💨  | Breathing Exercise  | 1 App  | ✅  | ✅  | ✅\n🔁  | Re-Intervention  | 1 App  | ♾️  | ♾️  | ♾️\n♾️  | Unlimited Apps  | ❌  | ✅  | ✅  | ✅\n📱  | Different Intervention Types  | ❌  | ✅  | N/A  | ✅\n🔄  | Intentional App Switching  | ❌  | ✅  | ✅  | ✅\n🔔  | “Don‘t Get Lost” Notifications  | ❌  | ✅  | N/A  | N/A\n\nUp to now, from various intervention types, Re-Intervention, the Phone Free Morning , scheduling, block sessions, Focus Filters, healthy alternatives, intention tracking, emotion tracking, integrations with Lengo and Structured, and the various lock functions, etc. – a ton of great tools have been added that weren’t factored into the original pricing. And there are more coming soon – we’re constantly working on it!\n\nIn parallel, we started developing browser extensions, a macOS version, and an Android version – all of which are included in every purchase, which helps fund the work done so far and the work still to come.\n\nAt the same time, our team has grown. Compared to others, we’re still a small team.\nBut now we have Android, Browser Extension, MacOS, and iOS developers, researchers & psychologists, backend developers, people in marketing and customer support, and a UX/UI design team – all people working passionately on this app and getting paid for it.\n\nSure, most of us still work part-time or mini-jobs, but this tiny indie app has grown massively. And with it, the effort to keep developing and maintaining it. That’s constant work, as operating systems evolve – and so do the needs of our users, which you can see on our feedback board and our roadmap.\n\nWe can only build a sustainable business long-term with subscriptions and recurring payments.\n\nWe believe our Pro subscriptions plans are still super affordable: for just $19 per year, a user saves an average of four weeks’ worth of time. We also offer a 50% discount for students.\n\nIf that’s still too much money for you, just send us a message – we’ll definitely find a solution!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIntervention not showing up when it should (https://tutorials.one-sec.app/en/articles/3262210)\nciteturn2search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.6 years ago; Crawled: last week; # Intervention not showing up when it should ...   * Intentional app switching time interval ... This is necessary, so that my app knows which app you intended to open, and can refer to the correct one after the breathing exercise.Open the Shortcuts app, go to the Automation Tab, and make sure that all Automations (especially for the app you intended to open right now) have the appropriate “one sec” Shortcut assigned to them.\n\n# Intervention not showing up when it should\n\nEdited Monday, January 20 2025\n\nTo be able to figure out what’s going on, please turn on one sec’s debug banner:\n\nOpen one sec → Customize → Advanced and turn on Show in Overview why automation is not triggered.\n\nAfter this option is enabled, you’ll see a banner at the top of the Overview page explaining why a certain automation was not triggered. There are many root causes, including:\n\n  * Intentional app switching time interval\n\n  * Focus Filter that allows using the app\n\n  * Intervention schedule that turns the intervention off for a certain hour\n\n  * Structured task color that allows using certain apps\n\n  * Automations won’t be triggered directly after booting the device for about 2 minutes.\n\n  * …\n\n# Double Check 🅰️ Open and 🅱️ Closing Actions\n\nPlease double-check that the 🅰️ Open action is only ran on app open, and the 🅱️ Closing action is only ran on app close.\n\n# Error message displayed?\n\nOpen the Shortcuts app, go to the Automation Tab, and check all your Automations (for app opening and closing) to make sure you’ve selected the “⚠️ Original App to be Opened”.\n\nThis is necessary, so that my app knows which app you intended to open, and can refer to the correct one after the breathing exercise.\n\nOpen the Shortcuts app, go to the Automation Tab, and make sure that all Automations (especially for the app you intended to open right now) have the appropriate “one sec” Shortcut assigned to them.\n\nOpening Automations should include the “🅰️ Activate one sec” Shortcut, whereas closing Automations should include the “🅱️ Log App Closing” Shortcut.\n\n# Using the free version of one sec?\n\nThe free version of one sec only allows to intervene one app. Please upgrade to one sec pro to configure multiple target apps.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOpal | Start Free Trial (https://opalapp.com/trial)\nciteturn2search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Get started with Opal Pro ... $99.99 billed annually. ... Opal browser extensions and iPhone app will stay in sync and block relevant apps and websites when needed. ...   * Free Trial Pricing All Features Focus Score Focus Sessions Focus Report Download for iPhone Download for Chrome\n\nGet started with Opal Pro\n\nLet’s start by signing in to your Opal account\n\n# Save 2hrs+ every day with Opal Pro\n\nMeasure your focus and block distractions\n\nImage\n\nToday: Start Free Trial\n\nBlock Apps automatically, get your detailed stats and stay on track to your dreams\n\nImage\n\nDay 6: See first results\n\nWe’ll send you a notification with a report to see how you improved this week\n\nImage\n\nDay 7: Trial Ends\n\nYour subscription will start this day. Cancel anytime before\n\n# Yearly + 7 day free\n\n# $8.29/month\n\n$99.99 billed annually. Cancel anytime.\n\nStart Free Week\n\nOR\n\n# Monthly + 3 day free\n\n# $19.99/month\n\nCancel anytime.\n\nStart Free 3 Days\n\n# Weekly + 3 day free\n\n# $9.99/week\n\nCancel anytime.\n\nStart Free 3 Days\n\n# Lifetime\n\n# $399\n\nKeep using Opal forever. All updates included.\n\nPurchase\n\nNote: purchasing Lifetime membership doesn't overwrite existing Apple subscription. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOpal FAQ | Why pay for Opal? (https://opalapp.com/help/why-pay-for-opal)\nciteturn2search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; ### Can I use my Opal Pro subscription on your new Android app?\nHelp Center\n\n# ❓\n\n# Why pay for Opal?\n\nOpal's mission is to empower people to focus. As a digital wellbeing company, we want to help you gain peace and balance with your use of digital technology. We help you block distractions via Sessions, Time Limits, and Open Limits; we also give you personalized insight with your Focus Score® and Focus Report. While you are welcome to use the free version of Opal, paying for Opal allows us to maintain and improve the product, and gives you access to Pro features on our iOS app, Mac App and via our Android App. If you purchase an annual or lifetime subscription on iOS, you are welcome to share your subscription with family members in the same household using Family Sharing.\n\n### What features are included with Opal Pro?\n\nThe free version of Opal gives you access to three recurring Focus Sessions, unlimited Focus Sessions that you can initiate immediately, our Time Limit and Open Limit feature, Focus Reports, and your day of Focus Score®. In contrast, Opal Pro grants you access to the following features:\n\n  * Unlimited Recurring Sessions that you can schedule in advance\n  * Our Allow List feature\n  * \"No way, I'm hardcore\" mode and so you're unable to cancel or take a break\n  * Focus Score® with History of your daily screen time\n\nTo subscribe to Opal Pro and see the benefits of each version of Opal, please head here or to the AppStore. If you have an Android device, you may purchase Opal Pro here.\n\n### Can I use my Opal Pro subscription on multiple devices?\n\nAbsolutely! There are a few addendums, however. To use your Opal Pro subscription purchased on iOS or Stripe on multiple devices, you'll first need to make sure you've signed up for an account using either your email or phone number. You can confirm by heading to your \"Settings\" on the iOS version of the app. Ensure that your subscription is associated with your account. If not, click on your \"Profile\" tab, then open your \"Settings\" (accessible from the upper right corner). From there, then scroll down and hit \"Restore Purchase\" to retrieve your subscription. Once that is complete, use the same credentials to log in on your other devices.\n\nMeanwhile, if you purchased your Opal Pro subscription via the PlayStore, please contact our Support team to ensure you may use it on your iOS devices.\n\n### Can I use my Opal Pro subscription on your new Android app?\n\nYes! That said, because the Android version of the app is currently being upgraded, our Support team will need to assist you with the setup if you transfer from iOS to Android. However, if you purchase the app via the PlayStore, it should work correctly on your Android device.\n\n### Do you offer subscription discounts for students and educators?\n\nWe offer discounts for students and educators. We know students can be strapped for cash, and we do not want to limit your access to our service. To receive a student or educator discount, please apply here. If you've submitted your information for a student or educator discount and have not heard back after 48 hours, please check your spam folder. If your discount still isn't appearing, please contact our Support team using the instructions here.\n\n### How can I get Opal Pro for free?\n\nIf you have five friends on the iOS app who create Opal accounts using your referral, you can earn one year of Opal Pro for free. There's more details on how to do that here. Currently, we do not yet support referrals on the Android version of the app, but that feature is coming soon!\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCut your screen time in half | one sec (https://one-sec.app/)\nciteturn2search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; ## one sec is the screen time app that truly works – scientifically. ... Yes, you have loads of possibilities to adapt one sec to your personal needs! - Schedule interruption timings: when and for how long should the intervention appear? - Choose from a variety of interruption types: what happens when an app or website is intervened? ... This site does not use cookies!\n\nCan I use sec across several devices?\n\nYes, one sec works cross-device. You can set up the app for iOS and Android devices, and use the browser extension on Windows, macOS and Linux computers. With the same account, you can log in to different smartphones, tablets and computers and use them simultaneously